# OPERATIONS §2.3 (M3): a base that doesn't load prints its one `refused: CODE message` line, as run prints it, "and
# nothing more": no warning, though spare is read by nothing; exit 1. amt is declared twice (LOAD-DUP, L §8.3), so
# run, any ask or none, prints the same line.
=== options check exit=1
=== model.tally
model household
  tally 2
  on 2026-03-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2027-12-31
  note "a model that declares an input twice (invented)"

source card "a card (invented)"

unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

input amt: money PLN
input spare: money PLN
input amt: money PLN

ask q: amt law 2026-03-01

version card_2026
  cite card
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  amt = 100.00 PLN "the card"
=== expect
refused: LOAD-DUP amt is declared twice ...
